  "article": [
    {
      "level": 2,
      "heading": "Overview",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "The App Store Server API limits the number of requests that you can submit to each endpoint within a specified timespan. The request limits apply per app.",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The following table lists the rate limits for each endpoint in the production environment, expressed in requests per second. The system enforces rate limits on an hourly basis.",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "| Endpoint | Rate limit (per second) |\n| --- | --- |\n| `Finish-Transaction` | 50 |\n| `Get-App-Transaction-Info` | 50 |\n| `Get-Transaction-Info` | 50 |\n| `Get-Transaction-History` | 50 |\n| `Get-Transaction-History-V1` | 50 |\n| `Get-All-Subscription-Statuses` | 50 |\n| `Send-Consumption-Information` | 50 |\n| `Send-Consumption-Information-V1` | 50 |\n| `Get-Notification-History` | 50 |\n| `Extend-a-Subscription-Renewal-Date` | 20 |\n| `Set-App-Account-Token` | 20 |\n| `Look-Up-Order-ID` | 10 |\n| `Get-Refund-History` | 10 |\n| `Get-Refund-History-V1` | 10 |\n| `Extend-Subscription-Renewal-Dates-for-All-Active-Subscribers` | 1 |\n| `Request-a-Test-Notification` | 1 |\n| `Get-Test-Notification-Status` | 1 |",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The rate limits in the sandbox environment are 10% of the limits in the table above.",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The App Store server may make adjustments to reduce or increase these rate limits as needed at any time.",
          "refs": []
        }
      ],
      "listItems": []
    },
    {
      "level": 3,
      "heading": "Handle exceeded rate limits gracefully",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "If you exceed a per-hour limit, the API rejects the request with an `HTTP` `429` response, with a `RateLimitExceededError` in the body.  Consider the following as you integrate the API:",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.appstoreserverapi/documentation/AppStoreServerAPI/RateLimitExceededError"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "listItems": [
        {
          "text": "If you periodically call the API, throttle your requests to avoid exceeding the per-hour limit for an endpoint.",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Manage the `HTTP` `429` `RateLimitExceededError` in your error-handling process. For example, log the failure and queue the job to process it again at a later time.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.appstoreserverapi/documentation/AppStoreServerAPI/RateLimitExceededError"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Check the `Retry-After` header if you receive the `HTTP` `429` error. This header contains a UNIX time, in milliseconds, that informs you when you can next send a request.",
          "refs": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
